We need to express: (e == null) => this.getLast() == null, and (e != null) => this.getLast().equals(e) (or ==? For objects, we can use .equals). In spec style, they use .equals for object equality. In earlier examples they used this.query(i).equals(...). So we should use .equals for non-null case.

Thus assert: (e == null => this.getLast() == null) && (e != null => this.getLast().equals(e))

But need parentheses: (e == null => this.getLast() == null) && (e != null => this.getLast().equals(e))

