analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment after the method offer.

The comment: "@@@ If the added element is null, then the last element in the list is also null; if the added element is not null, then it equals the last element in the list."

Method offer(E e) returns boolean add(e). It adds element to tail. So after operation, the last element (i.e., getLast()) should be null if e == null, else equals e.

We need to refer to observer methods: getLast() exists. Also size? Not needed.

So we need an assert that expresses: (e == null) => this.getLast() == null && (e != null) => this.getLast().equals(e). But careful: getLast returns E, could be null. So we can write: (e == null) => this.getLast() == null && (e != null) => this.getLast().equals(e). Need parentheses.

Spec syntax: (e == null) => this.getLast() == null && (e != null) => this.getLast().equals(e). However precedence: => lower than &&, so need parentheses: ((e == null) => this.getLast() == null) && ((e != null) => this.getLast().equals(e))

But also need to consider that after add, size increased, but not needed.

Thus final assert line:

assert ((e == null) => this.getLast() == null) && ((e != null) => this.getLast().equals(e));

Make sure to use \old? Not needed because we refer to after state.

Thus output code block.

assistantfinal<code>assert ((e == null) => this.getLast() == null) && ((e != null) => this.getLast().equals(e));</code>
